---
description: SwiftUI view rules for DJMemoryApp
globs: Sources/DJMemoryApp/**/*.swift
alwaysApply: false
---

## Aesthetic

A quiet native macOS system utility. Dense and compact, low corner radii, hairline dividers,
translucent sidebar, `NavigationSplitView` shell with traffic-light chrome. Inter throughout, strict
macOS light/dark system colors. Tabular numerals on every metric.

Not this: gradients, glow, drop shadows beyond system elevation, marketing copy, hero images,
photography, album art, emoji, animated flourishes.

## Tokens

Use the token layer only. **No hex literals in view files** — a `Color(hex:)` helper already exists,
do not add another. Per-app accents come from the accent map in `HANDOFF.md` §2; never hardcode one
inline.

## Structure

- One view per file, named after the screen or component it renders.
- Prefer `Table`, `ContentUnavailableView`, `Menu`, `.popover`, and other system controls over custom
  reimplementations. The add-app picker in §4.10 is a `Menu`/`.popover`, not a custom overlay.
- Extract a shared primitive only when it is used by two or more screens.
- Views read `AppModel` state; they do not compute aggregates. Aggregation belongs in `DJMemoryCore`.

## Previews

Every new view gets a `#Preview` per state in the relevant state matrix row (`HANDOFF.md` §5,
`HANDOFF-2-HOME.md`), in both light and dark. **Zero states are not optional** — a brand-new user has
no archived sets, no matched tracklists, no venues, and no tags, and every section must degrade to an
honest empty state that offers an action rather than rendering a blank panel.

## Accessibility

Preserve every existing `accessibilityIdentifier`; the smoke tests depend on them. New ones follow
the existing shape, e.g. `sidebar.addApp`, `sidebar.addApp.<appID>`.
